<p><strong>Why I don’t use a roller bag</strong></p>
<p>I have used roller bags in the past, the issue with them is that if you come across any rocky, or cobllestone roads, you will have a hard time. I personally believe that carrying is better overall, if you are physically capable of it. Now that we have our daughter and a stroller to bring, rolling bags just cause more issues than they are worth.</p>
<p>One lesson I learned is if you have a <strong>waist strap</strong> for your backpack, it is very worth using it as it takes a lot of the stress on your shoulders off.</p>
